# Defense-in-depth: production deploys run via GitHub Actions from a clean
# `actions/checkout`, so these untracked local files never reach that path.
# This only matters if someone ever runs `vercel deploy` from this working
# directory directly (bypassing the workflow) — keep it in sync with the
# untracked local content below.
reviews/img/_pending/
reviews/img/_review20/
reviews/img/_review30/
reviews/img/_reviewtech/
reviews/img/_superseded/
social-carousels/
tools/fonts/
tools/build_ready_to_post_today.py
tools/make_noah_carousels_v5.py
tools/make_noah_carousels_v6.py
tools/make_noah_carousels_x.py
tools/make_noah_premium_template_v2.py
tools/make_premium_viral_set.py
tools/make_social_carousels.py
tools/make_social_carousels_v2.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Internal files that must never be publicly served (audit 2026-09-23:
# REVIEWS-BACKUP.md, CLAUDE.md, tools/, .github/ etc. were live at 200).
# The GitHub Actions deploy runs `vercel deploy` from the checkout, so this
# file DOES apply to production.
